# Line-ending policy.
#
# Set 120 S3, 2026-08-11. This repo sets core.autocrlf=true and shipped
# no .gitattributes, so an ordinary `git rebase` rewrote already-stamped
# verification artifacts from LF to CRLF -- s3-verification.md grew
# 775 -> 780 bytes with no character changed -- and broke the
# artifact_sha256 the verification-integrity gate checks.
#
# The session constitution's rule is that a verification artifact is a
# raw record and is NEVER edited after it is written. Line-ending
# translation is an edit: it changes the bytes, and the bytes are what
# is stamped. So the artifacts the stamp covers are marked binary, which
# turns translation off in both directions.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the stamped artifacts rather than applied
# repo-wide. A whole-repo `* text=auto eol=lf` normalization is the
# right long-term answer and would touch every file in the tree, which
# is not a change to make inside a close.
docs/session-sets/**/s*-verification*.md -text
docs/session-sets/**/s*-issues*.json     -text
docs/session-sets/**/path-aware-critique.json -text
